{"duration": 75.813, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A dying soldier's face turned blue-violet, and doctors called it the purple death.", "start": 0.08, "end": 4.348}, {"beat": 0, "text": "France recorded influenza cases in April 1918.", "start": 4.568, "end": 8.051}, {"beat": 0, "text": "Three-quarters of French troops fell sick during that first wave.", "start": 8.271, "end": 11.303}, {"beat": 1, "text": "France had already lost nearly one point four million men killed or missing.", "start": 11.723, "end": 15.652}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Another four million French soldiers were wounded.", "start": 15.872, "end": 18.137}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Even so, French families kept sending their sons to the army.", "start": 18.357, "end": 21.705}, {"beat": 1, "text": "The first wave disrupted French military operations.", "start": 21.925, "end": 24.951}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Then a deadlier second wave arrived in autumn 1918.", "start": 25.371, "end": 28.716}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Among hospitalized soldiers, the second wave's death rate was far higher.", "start": 28.936, "end": 32.928}, {"beat": 2, "text": "October 1918 had the highest death rate of the whole pandemic.", "start": 33.148, "end": 36.955}, {"beat": 3, "text": "World War I caused poor food, crowded camps, and bad hygiene.", "start": 37.375, "end": 40.929}, {"beat": 3, "text": "Poor food and bad hygiene helped bacteria attack soldiers weakened by influenza.", "start": 41.149, "end": 45.863}, {"beat": 3, "text": "Most victims died after a long death bed.", "start": 46.083, "end": 48.347}, {"beat": 4, "text": "You see, a crowded hospital ward was like a packed bus: sickness had room to spread.", "start": 48.767, "end": 53.378}, {"beat": 5, "text": "The real reason: influenza weakened soldiers, and bacteria caused a second infection.", "start": 53.798, "end": 58.955}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Crowded camps and hospitals made that second infection deadly.", "start": 59.175, "end": 62.608}, {"beat": 6, "text": "Here is the twist: soldiers who caught flu in spring were protected from death that fall.", "start": 63.028, "end": 67.866}, {"beat": 6, "text": "Spring and summer exposure gave many soldiers protection against death.", "start": 68.086, "end": 71.86}, {"beat": 6, "text": "The first wave was a disaster, and also a shield.", "start": 72.08, "end": 74.693}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.145, "end": 0.195, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "dying", "start": 0.245, "end": 0.595, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "soldier's", "start": 0.645, "end": 1.07, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "face", "start": 1.12, "end": 1.37, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "turned", "start": 1.42, "end": 1.72, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "blue-violet,", "start": 1.77, "end": 2.695, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "and", "start": 2.745, "end": 2.82, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "doctors", "start": 2.845, "end": 3.27, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "called", "start": 3.32, "end": 3.57, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "it", "start": 3.595, "end": 3.645, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "the", "start": 3.67, "end": 3.72, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "purple", "start": 3.77, "end": 4.095, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "death.", "start": 4.145, "end": 4.475, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "France", "start": 4.658, "end": 4.983, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "recorded", "start": 5.033, "end": 5.483, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "influenza", "start": 5.533, "end": 6.033, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "cases", "start": 6.083, "end": 6.758, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "in", "start": 6.833, "end": 6.933, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "April", "start": 6.983, "end": 7.233, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "1918.", "start": 7.283, "end": 8.109, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "Three-quarters", "start": 8.361, "end": 8.911, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "of", "start": 8.936, "end": 8.986, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "French", "start": 9.036, "end": 9.236, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "troops", "start": 9.286, "end": 9.561, "l